    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is a deadlock?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A deadlock occurs when two or more threads wait for each other to release resources, causing all to wait indefinitely."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Deadlock requires four conditions: mutual exclusion, hold and wait, no preemption, circular wait. Prevent by acquiring locks in consistent order."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Deadlock Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "// Deadlock scenario\nobject lock1 = new();\\object lock2 = new();\n\n// Thread 1\nlock (lock1) {\n    lock (lock2) { /* deadlock */ }\n}\n\n// Thread 2\nlock (lock2) {\n    lock (lock1) { /* deadlock */ }\n}\n\n// Fix: consistent lock order\nlock (lock1) {\n    lock (lock2) { /* safe */ }\n}"
      }
    },
